--TEST--
`self`, `static` and `parent` written at the top level of a file are `E0303` at each of the four sites that resolve a class side — a class constant, a static property, a static call and `new` — while a written class name on the left of the same four is not reported, `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/refused-in-expression-position
// `self`, `static` and `parent` each name a class through the declaration
// they are written in. At the top level of a file there is no declaration to
// name one, so each site that resolves a class side has nothing to resolve.
// Before this was reported, all four recorded no entry at all and `nvs-ir`
// panicked naming the table it found empty.
class Target {
    public const int LIMIT = 1;

    public static int $count = 0;

    public static function twice(int $n): int {
        return $n * 2;
    }
}

echo self::LIMIT, "\n";
echo self::$count, "\n";
echo parent::twice(2), "\n";
var $made = new static();
// The control: a written class name on the left of the same four spellings
// resolves, so none of them is reported and the expectation below carries
// exactly four diagnostics.
echo Target::LIMIT, Target::$count, Target::twice(2), "\n";
var $ok = new Target();
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `self` used outside any class
   --> %s:18:6
   |
18 | echo self::LIMIT, "\n";
   |      ^^^^ no enclosing class
   = help: `self`, `static` and `parent` each name a class through the declaration they are written in — name the class itself, or move this inside one

error[E0303]: `self` used outside any class
   --> %s:19:6
   |
19 | echo self::$count, "\n";
   |      ^^^^ no enclosing class
   = help: `self`, `static` and `parent` each name a class through the declaration they are written in — name the class itself, or move this inside one

error[E0303]: `parent` used outside any class
   --> %s:20:6
   |
20 | echo parent::twice(2), "\n";
   |      ^^^^^^ no enclosing class
   = help: `self`, `static` and `parent` each name a class through the declaration they are written in — name the class itself, or move this inside one

error[E0303]: `static` used outside any class
   --> %s:21:13
   |
21 | var $made = new static();
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^ no enclosing class
   = help: `self`, `static` and `parent` each name a class through the declaration they are written in — name the class itself, or move this inside one

